From eff3dfa06d9bece7c666a5daa5c71b0abf79e0de Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ash Pera <ashley.pera@noaa.gov>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 12:04:22 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 08/18] noahmpdrv: hand the atmosphere the water Noah-MP
 removed, not latent heat / con_hvap

evap was latent_heat_total/density/con_hvap (2.5e6 J/kg), while Noah-MP
removes the water with its own hvap = 2.5104e6 and, over frozen surfaces,
hsub = 2.844e6. The atmosphere therefore received 0.4 % more water than
unfrozen land lost and 14 % more over snow and frozen ground.

Use the water flux Noah-MP itself computes, (ecan+etran+edir)/density, as the
WRF, HRLDAS, MPAS and LIS Noah-MP drivers do (QFX). Noah-MP's latent heat flux
is unchanged. The host's latent-heat output, rho*con_hvap*evap, now follows
the water: up to 12 % lower where sublimation dominates, -4.2 % over
snow-covered land in a 24-h C96 forecast.

Measured with in-model meters (C96 control_p8_ugwpv1): the atmosphere gained
+0.07 to +0.10 % of global precipitation more water than the land lost; with
the fix the two agree to machine precision. Note this lowers the water flux
over frozen surfaces by up to 12 %. See also NCAR/ccpp-physics#582.
---
 physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/noahmpdrv.F90 | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/noahmpdrv.F90 b/physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/noahmpdrv.F90
index 5506fc34..bd9468e3 100644
--- a/physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/noahmpdrv.F90
+++ b/physics/SFC_Models/Land/Noahmp/noahmpdrv.F90
@@ -1523,7 +1523,8 @@ end subroutine noahmpdrv_timestep_init
 !  --- change units for output
 !
       hflx(i) = hflx(i) / density / con_cp
-      evap(i) = evap(i) / density / con_hvap
+      ! the water Noah-MP removed (its own hvap/hsub), not latent heat / con_hvap
+      evap(i) = (ecan(i) + etran(i) + edir(i)) / density
 
 !
 !  --- calculate potential evaporation using noah code
